WEBVTT

01:46.147 --> 01:48.566
<i>Half a second
before the brain processes "now."</i>

01:49.484 --> 01:52.862
<i>It's a divine state the person themselves
isn't even conscious of.</i>

01:53.822 --> 01:55.406
<i>Grasping that moment.</i>

01:56.199 --> 02:01.412
<i>Every person gives off this "signal"
half a second before.</i>

02:02.580 --> 02:05.917
<i>Hands in the pockets
and constantly observing,</i>

02:07.001 --> 02:09.504
<i>watching for the "now"
that's about to come.</i>

02:10.713 --> 02:14.092
<i>Just like a sword in its sheath,</i>

02:14.634 --> 02:16.761
<i>waiting for the moment it's drawn.</i>

02:18.012 --> 02:20.056
<i>The "now" that could come even now.</i>

02:21.474 --> 02:25.270
<i>Even now, that "now"
could come right after now.</i>

02:30.275 --> 02:32.193
Oh, that's right.

02:33.778 --> 02:35.238
Huh? What?

02:36.281 --> 02:40.618
A father and son, blood relatives,
probing each other's intentions.

02:41.703 --> 02:43.204
But this isn't quite right.

02:44.789 --> 02:46.958
What's he doing?

02:48.042 --> 02:48.960
That's enough.

02:51.045 --> 02:53.548
There's no need to wait
until the half-second

02:53.631 --> 02:54.966
before deciding to attack.

02:55.049 --> 02:57.468
<i>Why's he doing this?</i>

02:58.386 --> 02:59.429
I'll tell you.

03:00.096 --> 03:01.222
Tell me?

03:01.306 --> 03:06.227
No need for anything so rushed
as the half-second before "activation."

03:07.562 --> 03:08.479
Five seconds!

03:10.648 --> 03:15.987
I'll give you a countdown myself,
five seconds before I attack.

03:16.070 --> 03:20.241
What?! A countdown? Are you...

03:20.825 --> 03:22.577
I'll bend each finger,

03:22.660 --> 03:26.122
and once my hand transforms into a fist,

03:26.206 --> 03:27.248
I'll let it loose.

03:28.583 --> 03:30.919
<i>They were to probe
each other's trigger moment,</i>

03:31.002 --> 03:33.755
<i>but it's turned into
a completely different game.</i>

03:34.631 --> 03:37.759
The physical preparation.
The mental preparation.

03:38.843 --> 03:40.136
Prepare yourself.

03:40.220 --> 03:44.265
Hold on there! I haven't agreed yet!

03:45.183 --> 03:46.267
Five.

03:48.353 --> 03:49.520
Four.

03:50.188 --> 03:51.522
<i>What is he playing at?!</i>

03:52.232 --> 03:53.066
Three.

03:55.693 --> 03:56.527
Two.

03:58.112 --> 03:59.030
One!

03:59.656 --> 04:00.531
There!

04:01.115 --> 04:02.200
<i>Now!</i>

04:04.118 --> 04:07.664
<i>The fastest "fist draw,"
faster than a fraction of a second.</i>

04:07.747 --> 04:11.000
<i>Ultimately, the young man's body
decided the fastest move</i>

04:11.084 --> 04:13.253
<i>was not to pull his hands
out of his pockets,</i>

04:13.336 --> 04:15.546
<i>but to leave his hands at the same height</i>

04:15.630 --> 04:18.299
<i>and to lower his body
in order to draw out his hands.</i>

04:19.759 --> 04:23.054
<i>It is similar to the body movement
and rationale of</i> iai,

04:23.137 --> 04:25.348
<i>the art of drawing a sword.</i>

04:25.431 --> 04:29.894
<i>Where the hilt remains grazing the floor,
while the hip is turned in order to draw.</i>

04:42.198 --> 04:45.827
<i>It was the greatest gift that evening
from his son, Baki.</i>

04:45.910 --> 04:48.913
<i>The upper jaw and lower jaw...</i>

04:50.290 --> 04:53.084
<i>A secret move imitating
the grinding motion of tiger jaws.</i>

04:57.255 --> 04:58.840
<i>Aptly named, Tiger King!</i>

04:59.590 --> 05:00.925
<i>A brilliant feat!</i>

05:05.638 --> 05:09.892
Letting yourself get beaten
by such a classic fighting move.

05:09.976 --> 05:12.854
You must be getting slow
in your old age, Ogre.

05:14.689 --> 05:16.357
But still,

05:17.317 --> 05:22.447
Baki, you're incredibly strong, kid.

05:24.157 --> 05:28.870
<i>He could clearly feel
his father's thick neck beneath his knee.</i>

05:29.746 --> 05:33.374
<i>He could clearly feel his father's arm
robbed of its freedom.</i>

05:34.584 --> 05:38.629
<i>Dad is clearly under me right now!</i>

05:41.716 --> 05:44.135
<i>A sense of achievement
greater than himself,</i>

05:44.218 --> 05:46.137
<i>and an unease larger than life.</i>

05:46.804 --> 05:48.639
<i>He felt both!</i>

05:50.141 --> 05:53.353
Ogre, you were way too careless.

05:54.228 --> 05:57.607
<i>Baki's a monster with your DNA.</i>

05:57.690 --> 06:00.151
<i>You underestimated him way too much.</i>

06:00.234 --> 06:01.652
You idiot.

06:04.072 --> 06:06.616
Dad, can you hear me?

06:10.745 --> 06:13.414
"I wondered what you'd do."

06:13.498 --> 06:16.417
"This is exactly the kind of trick
I'd expect you to pull."

06:17.877 --> 06:20.671
Dad, I bet it's pretty hard for you

06:20.755 --> 06:22.924
to say that kind of thing
in this position.

06:25.259 --> 06:27.553
Don't pull this shit, Dad!

06:27.637 --> 06:30.181
You'd better not let it end like this!

06:30.807 --> 06:32.934
I won't fuckin' let you!

06:33.017 --> 06:34.685
Try and make a comeback, dammit!

06:34.769 --> 06:38.689
That's what Yujiro Hanma would do,
goddammit!

06:42.276 --> 06:45.154
<i>Baki, don't push your luck.</i>

06:45.238 --> 06:47.448
<i>Your papa's not that weak, you know.</i>

06:55.540 --> 06:57.834
"Okay"?

06:59.794 --> 07:02.964
<i>He's lifting his right arm.</i>

07:03.548 --> 07:04.465
<i>Wait.</i>

07:04.549 --> 07:07.301
<i>What would be the point
of lifting his arm?</i>

07:08.803 --> 07:10.888
<i>What does it signify? Confidence?</i>

07:10.972 --> 07:12.765
<i>It can't be baseless.</i>

07:12.849 --> 07:15.726
<i>Is he agitated or confused?
I can't predict what he'll do!</i>

07:16.352 --> 07:19.021
<i>He's in a completely helpless position.</i>

07:19.105 --> 07:21.732
<i>What the hell could he do
with his right arm?</i>

07:28.448 --> 07:30.741
- A crack in the ground!
- Whoa! Look!

07:32.326 --> 07:33.870
It's buried in the ground!

07:33.953 --> 07:36.747
His arm is buried in the asphalt!

07:49.844 --> 07:51.095
He's not human!

07:51.179 --> 07:52.763
He's too damn strong!

07:54.432 --> 07:56.267
Punching through the asphalt...

07:56.851 --> 07:59.020
That's a hell of an idea.

07:59.687 --> 08:02.607
<i>If it hadn't been Yujiro Hanma,
that'd be impossible.</i>

08:03.107 --> 08:04.817
<i>That's for sure.</i>

08:04.901 --> 08:07.028
<i>That's absolutely right.</i>

08:07.111 --> 08:12.033
<i>Ogre's idea of the ground and asphalt
isn't the same as everyone else's.</i>

08:12.617 --> 08:15.161
<i>If you fight on top of gelatin or agar,</i>

08:15.244 --> 08:18.039
<i>the pinning move wouldn't be
a pinning move at all.</i>

08:20.541 --> 08:23.044
Sorry, Dad. That truly was

08:23.961 --> 08:26.797
a typical trick that I'd pull.

08:29.342 --> 08:32.720
But you see, this fight...

08:33.346 --> 08:36.265
I've gotta win it even if I pee my pants.

08:38.893 --> 08:41.896
Are you sure, boss?

08:42.897 --> 08:45.816
It's been a while since it started.

08:56.452 --> 08:57.328
What has?

08:57.912 --> 09:02.333
I mean... the news and stuff
are making a big deal about it.

09:05.628 --> 09:09.840
You wanna watch
some family's father-son fight?

09:12.176 --> 09:13.052
Well,

09:14.470 --> 09:17.014
I wanna watch!

09:20.935 --> 09:21.769
Me too.

09:24.480 --> 09:25.606
<i>Whaddya think, everyone?</i>

09:26.774 --> 09:28.609
<i>Isn't my dad pretty awesome?</i>

09:29.569 --> 09:34.615
<i>He's so strong that even I,
Baki Hanma, peed my pants.</i>

09:36.242 --> 09:37.785
You did good up to Tiger King.

09:39.453 --> 09:43.124
You cry and wet yourself so easily.

09:43.833 --> 09:46.460
Yeah, that's right. That's exactly right.

09:47.420 --> 09:52.133
I cry. I wet myself. I deceive. I trick.

09:53.050 --> 09:54.135
You just realized that?

09:55.761 --> 09:59.640
<i>I'll get the win no matter what it takes.</i>

10:02.351 --> 10:04.895
<i>Whether I've gotta cry.
Whether I've gotta pee myself.</i>

10:06.981 --> 10:09.525
<i>Whether I've gotta deceive.
Whether I've gotta trick.</i>

10:13.112 --> 10:14.363
What was that?!

10:14.864 --> 10:17.283
A side roll kick?

10:17.867 --> 10:19.785
To cross counter?!

10:23.372 --> 10:24.457
He landed!

10:24.957 --> 10:26.292
He wasn't hit?!

10:27.001 --> 10:28.544
Damn good, Dad.

10:33.382 --> 10:35.301
Nice. That's good enough.

10:36.344 --> 10:39.221
<i>What's going on? His expression is kind.</i>

10:40.306 --> 10:44.060
<i>I never knew he could look like that!</i>

10:46.562 --> 10:52.276
Half-assed attempts won't wake
the genes asleep within you.

10:52.902 --> 10:55.154
I'm prepared to slap them awake.

10:56.781 --> 10:59.325
<i>The Hanma blood... DNA...</i>

11:00.409 --> 11:01.827
<i>It won't be long now.</i>

11:03.412 --> 11:05.831
<i>He's gonna end it.</i>

11:06.666 --> 11:08.334
<i>My son, Baki...</i>

11:09.710 --> 11:12.838
<i>My life had been filled with boredom.</i>

11:14.173 --> 11:15.049
His back!

11:15.132 --> 11:16.592
- It's the Ogre!
- The <i>oni</i>'s face!

11:17.301 --> 11:19.845
<i>The one who gave me my first thrill</i>

11:20.554 --> 11:23.099
<i>could naturally only be my own son.</i>

11:23.182 --> 11:26.102
He made it weep.

11:26.185 --> 11:28.771
Is he really going to do that?

11:28.854 --> 11:29.855
Huh? What?

11:29.939 --> 11:31.607
He's crazy!

11:32.400 --> 11:33.359
Live.

11:35.611 --> 11:37.863
Thank you for the wonderful evening.

11:39.448 --> 11:42.284
Make your father happy!

12:24.744 --> 12:26.120
A coincidence, yes,

12:26.203 --> 12:29.457
but who'd have thought a chamber
of this size still remained?

12:30.332 --> 12:32.501
Professor Chris, what is this?

12:34.295 --> 12:36.672
At first look, it seems ominous.

12:37.214 --> 12:39.341
It looks like a drawing of a demon.

12:40.134 --> 12:42.052
What bothers me is,

12:42.887 --> 12:45.639
why the back?

12:46.390 --> 12:49.643
From an anatomical perspective,
it's very exact.

12:50.811 --> 12:55.566
The arms, shoulders,
and from the waist to the feet.

12:56.525 --> 13:00.154
But why on earth is just the back
like a demon's face?

13:01.155 --> 13:04.033
Professor, is this
a kind of religious image?

13:09.622 --> 13:12.166
This is the same thing.

13:12.249 --> 13:14.835
But the background is different.

13:15.836 --> 13:16.837
They're weapons.

13:17.755 --> 13:19.632
Tips of various sizes.

13:20.424 --> 13:22.218
They're weapons pointed at him.

13:23.052 --> 13:26.263
No. Considering the variety and number,

13:26.806 --> 13:30.434
they represent weaponry, armaments.

13:30.935 --> 13:32.728
This is amazing.

13:32.812 --> 13:34.605
Such incredible fighting power.

13:35.272 --> 13:38.025
True. That's a heck of a lot of weapons.

13:39.902 --> 13:41.612
That's not what this means.

13:42.488 --> 13:45.866
It's saying that this devil
had such great fighting power

13:46.742 --> 13:49.662
that this much weaponry
had to be readied to face it.

13:50.704 --> 13:52.790
That's for sure.

14:05.135 --> 14:08.097
Whoa! That car's been totally destroyed!

14:08.180 --> 14:10.057
<i>You're gonna kill your son.</i>

14:18.816 --> 14:21.443
<i>The utter destructive power
to strike a human</i>

14:21.527 --> 14:24.947
<i>and also completely crush
a large van in the same punch.</i>

14:25.739 --> 14:28.701
<i>It was a little late,
but Baki realized something.</i>

14:29.660 --> 14:32.079
<i>"Yes, what I am fighting now</i>

14:32.872 --> 14:35.082
<i>is an ultra-force
that frightens entire nations."</i>

14:37.626 --> 14:42.047
"<i>Even if I gave it everything I've got,
there's no way I could defeat it.</i>"

14:47.136 --> 14:48.888
<i>This feeling,</i>

14:48.971 --> 14:50.764
<i>this sweet numbness,</i>

14:50.848 --> 14:52.975
<i>I can feel it.</i>

14:53.058 --> 14:54.476
<i>Is this the Brain Drug?</i>

14:55.269 --> 14:56.312
<i>It itches.</i>

14:57.062 --> 14:59.231
<i>It must be showing up on my back...</i>

14:59.982 --> 15:01.734
<i>That tiny</i> oni...

15:02.693 --> 15:05.446
<i>That's right. I did everything I could.</i>

15:06.238 --> 15:08.532
<i>I've given it everything I've got.</i>

15:08.616 --> 15:09.783
<i>Even my pee.</i>

15:10.701 --> 15:12.745
<i>I squeezed out everything I had.</i>

15:16.707 --> 15:17.833
<i>I've had it.</i>

15:20.127 --> 15:21.670
That's enough.

15:26.800 --> 15:27.843
You wanna continue?

15:30.721 --> 15:31.764
You really are

15:32.723 --> 15:35.267
a father so strong that it makes me proud.

15:41.774 --> 15:44.777
Continue? Or let go?

15:49.615 --> 15:52.242
I know full well it won't work,

15:52.910 --> 15:58.540
but to hear you ask me that directly,
Dad, that's just so...

16:00.626 --> 16:01.543
Dad...

16:02.127 --> 16:03.087
For me...

16:06.715 --> 16:07.549
Who's that?

16:15.641 --> 16:20.312
Have you become lost, Yuichiro Hanma?

16:20.396 --> 16:21.689
- Huh?
- What is it?

16:21.772 --> 16:23.315
-"Yuichiro"?
- Who's that?

16:23.941 --> 16:26.318
Grandpa?!

16:31.115 --> 16:32.324
You haven't changed.

16:32.408 --> 16:34.827
His shoulders are so broad.

16:37.413 --> 16:40.916
My child, struggling against his own.

16:43.919 --> 16:45.337
Baki, my boy.

16:46.672 --> 16:47.840
Yes?

16:48.424 --> 16:50.843
You can win.

16:53.220 --> 16:54.430
He can see him?

16:55.305 --> 16:58.434
What? See what?

16:58.517 --> 17:02.938
The man who defeated America
before Yujiro did.

17:03.022 --> 17:05.649
Defeated America?

17:05.733 --> 17:08.944
I don't quite understand what you mean.

17:10.112 --> 17:12.281
Yuichiro Hanma.

17:12.364 --> 17:15.034
Yujiro Hanma's biological father.

17:17.369 --> 17:20.497
<i>It was the Battle of Okinawa
during the Pacific War.</i>

17:21.582 --> 17:25.169
<i>From April 1, 1945,</i>

17:25.252 --> 17:27.921
<i>when the U.S. army
started its invasion of Okinawa,</i>

17:28.005 --> 17:32.634
<i>until the signing of the surrender
on September 7 in Kadena,</i>

17:32.718 --> 17:37.514
<i>were six months of hell
called the Battle of Okinawa.</i>

17:37.598 --> 17:39.850
<i>But that's not what really happened.</i>

17:40.476 --> 17:43.604
<i>Twelve kilometers off
the northeastern shore</i>

17:43.687 --> 17:45.522
<i>of the main island of Okinawa,</i>

17:45.606 --> 17:47.775
<i>there's a puny solitary island,</i>

17:47.858 --> 17:51.403
<i>less than a kilometer in circumference,
so small it's not on any map.</i>

17:52.863 --> 17:55.199
<i>Into that small area,</i>

17:55.282 --> 18:00.412
<i>more than 1,000 tons of explosives
were launched in total.</i>

18:00.996 --> 18:02.623
A thousand tons?!

18:02.706 --> 18:05.751
That many explosives
were used on Japan's army?

18:05.834 --> 18:08.462
Not on the Imperial Japanese Army.

18:08.545 --> 18:10.422
Nor on the locals.

18:11.840 --> 18:15.844
<i>It was used on one single man,
Yuichiro Hanma.</i>

18:17.513 --> 18:19.932
<i>Bombardment from naval guns on the ocean.</i>

18:20.808 --> 18:22.935
<i>Aerial bombing from the sky.</i>

18:23.644 --> 18:27.439
<i>After so much bombing
that even the island's shape was changed,</i>

18:28.440 --> 18:29.942
<i>they landed.</i>

18:30.651 --> 18:34.780
<i>The mission given to the soldiers
was simply to confirm his corpse.</i>

18:35.322 --> 18:38.200
<i>It felt like a walk in the park,
but only briefly.</i>

18:38.283 --> 18:40.452
<i>Standing there</i>

18:41.245 --> 18:44.790
<i>was the Japanese man they were meant
to bring back as a corpse.</i>

18:45.958 --> 18:50.087
<i>Dangling from his right hand
with his neck hanging at a funny angle,</i>

18:50.170 --> 18:54.216
<i>was the soldier who had been in the rear.</i>

18:55.801 --> 19:00.722
<i>The commander of this operation,
Major General James, said this.</i>

19:00.806 --> 19:03.183
Even against that battleship Yamato,

19:03.267 --> 19:06.228
we only suffered 12 casualties
before it was sunk!

19:06.311 --> 19:09.731
How the hell can we be disgraced like that
by a single monkey?!

19:10.440 --> 19:13.360
<i>"That man isn't any damn monkey."</i>

19:13.861 --> 19:17.573
<i>The young officers swallowed their words.</i>

19:18.824 --> 19:21.243
This isn't a matter of efficiency.

19:21.326 --> 19:25.747
This is a matter of protecting
the dignity of our proud Marine Corps!

19:26.999 --> 19:32.379
<i>Of all things, James asked
Supreme Commander MacArthur</i>

19:32.462 --> 19:36.341
<i>for permission to use an atom bomb.</i>

19:36.842 --> 19:38.927
That's ridiculous! Absolutely ridiculous!

19:39.678 --> 19:43.265
Thirty-eight days earlier,

19:43.348 --> 19:47.227
there was a broadcast by the Emperor
announcing the end of the war.

19:47.311 --> 19:49.521
There was no way
permission would be granted.

19:49.605 --> 19:53.275
Then that night, after the order
had been given to cease the operation,

19:54.026 --> 19:56.278
<i>that's when it happened.</i>

19:57.696 --> 20:01.783
<i>After hearing the sound of an impact,
what the soldiers saw</i>

20:02.868 --> 20:08.373
<i>was the corpse of Major General James
thrust deep into the deck of the ship.</i>

20:08.874 --> 20:14.296
<i>There was only one soldier
who witnessed this event.</i>

20:15.255 --> 20:17.549
<i>While he was relaxing on the deck,</i>

20:18.342 --> 20:21.261
<i>he was shocked by a massive crash.</i>

20:21.345 --> 20:25.807
<i>When the soldier turned around,
he clearly saw it.</i>

20:26.892 --> 20:32.189
<i>The sight of a fiercely brutal</i> oni

20:32.272 --> 20:34.566
<i>about to calmly walk away.</i>

20:35.234 --> 20:39.029
<i>It was a sudden, grisly end
for the operation's commander.</i>

20:39.529 --> 20:44.576
<i>The Iowa battleship's deck
was 233 millimeters thick.</i>

20:45.118 --> 20:49.039
<i>Apparently, the crew members
were deeply frightened.</i>

20:50.165 --> 20:54.086
"<i>What kind of power was used
to throw him down like that?!"</i>

20:54.878 --> 20:57.714
"<i>Was this some kind of technique?"</i>

20:57.798 --> 20:58.757
<i>"An</i> oni!"

20:59.466 --> 21:02.094
<i>"What kind of monster is it?"</i>

21:04.680 --> 21:06.348
<i>He hadn't left.</i>

21:07.391 --> 21:12.854
<i>Until the more than 2,000 crew members
all assembled on the deck,</i>

21:13.563 --> 21:16.525
<i>the</i> oni <i>had hidden himself.</i>

21:17.943 --> 21:23.282
On that ship, Yuichiro used
a very mysterious technique.

21:23.991 --> 21:27.369
I personally didn't see it, but...

21:28.245 --> 21:32.207
<i>Given the mere fact that the more
than 2,000 crew members of the Iowa</i>

21:32.291 --> 21:35.627
<i>surged over its sides
into the ocean to escape,</i>

21:35.711 --> 21:39.464
<i>I think you can understand
how dreadful it was.</i>

21:40.716 --> 21:42.301
<i>In a mere few minutes,</i>

21:42.384 --> 21:47.472
<i>the entire crew abandoned
the Iowa battleship, their nation's pride.</i>

21:48.932 --> 21:54.396
<i>It's really no wonder
that they say he defeated America.</i>

21:55.105 --> 21:58.108
What kind of technique was it?

21:58.191 --> 22:01.028
This is what the technique is called.

22:01.862 --> 22:03.322
"Dress."

22:06.867 --> 22:08.410
Damn, he disappeared.

22:10.787 --> 22:14.041
After seeing that face I hadn't seen
in a while, I remembered something.

22:15.208 --> 22:17.127
Dad's best technique.
